# File and folder naming

Apply when creating, renaming, or moving code. Match the target directory’s existing style.

## Rules (strict)

- **Folders**: `kebab-case` only (`quote-items-grid/`, `product-lookup-dialog/`).
- **Source files**: `kebab-case` only (`quote-items-grid.tsx`, `use-grid-columns.tsx`, `action-renderer.tsx`).
- Do **not** use PascalCase or camelCase in paths (`QuoteItemsGrid.tsx`, `quoteItemsGrid/`, `useCheckProductCode.tsx` are wrong).

This rule covers **paths only**. TypeScript/React identifier style (components, hooks, types, variables) is defined in **ai-standing-orders.mdc** and **components-ui.mdc** — not here.

## Examples

```text
# Good paths
quote-items-grid/quote-items-grid.tsx
quote-items-grid/hooks/use-check-product-code.tsx
quote-items-grid/components/renderers/action-renderer.tsx

# Bad paths
quoteItemsGrid/QuoteItemsGrid.tsx
hooks/useCheckProductCode.tsx
SmartCalculationsActive.tsx
```

## Renames

- Use `git mv` for path changes.
- Update barrel `index.ts` re-exports and every import.
- Remove stale duplicate folders left after renames.

## Exceptions

- `src/components/ui/*` — keep existing lowercase shadcn-style names unless adding a new file (then prefer `kebab-case`).
- `supabase/migrations/` — `YYYYMMDDHHmmss_description.sql` (UTC).
- Third-party/vendor files — do not rename.
